## Description

This analytic detects **Microsoft Office applications spawning PowerShell**, a behavior that is uncommon during normal office productivity workflows and frequently associated with phishing attacks, malicious Office macros, and malware execution.

Rather than detecting a specific malicious file or hash, this rule identifies suspicious **parent-child process relationships**, making it a valuable behavior-based detection.

Even though Microsoft Office is not installed within this lab environment, this detection demonstrates how Security Operations Centers (SOCs) identify malicious process chains in production environments.

