# Analyst Notes

This detection is an example of **behavior-based detection engineering** rather than signature-based detection.

Modern attackers frequently use phishing emails containing malicious Microsoft Office documents that execute PowerShell through VBA macros or embedded scripts. Detecting the relationship between the parent Office process and the child PowerShell process provides high-fidelity visibility into this attack technique.

Although the laboratory environment cannot generate this telemetry due to the absence of Microsoft Office, documenting and validating the analytic demonstrates an understanding of enterprise detection engineering practices and common attacker tradecraft.
